Interview Answer

What is curl?
"curl is a command-line tool used to transfer data to and from a server. It is widely used to test REST APIs, send HTTP requests (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE), and verify web services."

What is wget?
"wget is a command-line utility used to download files from the internet. It supports resuming interrupted downloads and is commonly used in Linux and DevOps to download software packages, binaries, and scripts."

Interview answer

curl and wget are both command-line tools used to download files from the internet. However, curl is mainly used for transferring data and testing APIs, while wget is mainly designed for downloading files
and websites, with features like recursive downloading and automatic resume.


Examples

Download a file using curl:

curl -O https://example.com/file.txt

Download the same file using wget:

wget https://example.com/file.txt

Rule to remember:

API calls → curl
File downloads → wget

Option	Purpose
-O	Save with original filename
-o filename	Save with a custom filename
-L	Follow redirects
-C -	Resume an interrupted download
-#	Show a progress bar
-I	Fetch only the HTTP headers
curl -o myfile.txt https://example.com/file.txt
curl -L -O https://example.com/download
wget -P /home/ec2-user/ https://example.com/project.zip
wget -O myproject.zip https://example.com/project.zip

